<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.893 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.893 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due February 20 was 2.893 percent, down from 2.911 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.4 billion of 182-day T-bills due May 22, 1997 was 3.035 percent, down from 3.081 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due November 13, 1997 was 3.340 percent, down from 3.350 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$700 million three-month, C$225 million six-month and C$150 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.25 billion of C$7.8 billion of bills due Nov 28.</p>
